const LOG_MODEL='Glass’s return is often told as a contest between one man and nature, but that version strips away the network that made his journey possible. Before the attack, he brought his experience to the table as a member of an expedition. After he was abandoned, he had to fend for himself, and practical knowledge came into play in a pinch. Still, by no stretch of the imagination did he create the conditions of his survival alone. He stuck with the journey, battled against the elements, and finally reached a fort built and occupied by other people. His endurance matters, but so does the world he returned to.';
